```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
April 11, 2024
The property is currently assessed as residential and is located within the A-2 -
Agricultural Zone District. It is accessed on the north side from US Highway 30 and is
bordered by US Highway 30 to the north, undeveloped right-of-way to the east, Tracts
25 and 26, Mesa Tracts 2nd Filing to the south, and a portion of Tract 6, Mesa Tracts
and Tract 1, Long View Subdivision to the west.
Trystin and Mike Green were introduced and said that the types of trailers being sold
would include utility and enclosed trailers.
Chairman Caughey opened the Public Hearing. Ray Martin, owner of adjoining tracts
said his concerns are that eventually he will annex his property into the City and would
create residential and commercial parcels. He asked that any development along
there include adequate fencing so there was some barrier between the residences
and other parcels. Mr. Arnold responded that buffering and landscaping will be
addressed in the Site Plan approval process and that the proposal fits into the
PlanCheyenne land use designation.
A motion was made by John Watkins, seconded by Jack Stadel to
approve a Zone Change from A-2 to MU for Tract 5, Mesa Tracts,
Laramie County, WY. Vote 4-0.
Caughey, Stadel, Watkins, Gaspar
Aye:
Smith
Excused:
3.
Public Hearing regarding a review and recommendation of the
Preliminary Development Plan and a Subdivision Permit and Plat for
Pita Ranch, 2nd Filing, situated in a portion of the N1/2 of the SE1/4 of
Section 34, Township 14 North, Range 63 West, and a portion of
Tract 1, Pita Ranch, Laramie County, WY.
24 - 178
PZ-24-00017,18 LCPC Staff Report 04.11.24
Attachments:
Sonny Keen, Associate Planner, said that Steil Surveying, on behalf G & G
Enterprises, has submitted Preliminary Development Plan and Subdivision Permit
and Plat applications for this property located on the west side of County Road 146,
and south of Iron Horse Road. The application has been submitted to subdivide the
40.63 combined acreage into seven (7) residential tracts averaging 5.25 - 8 acres
each.  These applications were filed concurrently which was allowable under the
Laramie County Land Use Regulations in force at the time of submission.  Both
applications have been combined into one staff report for ease of presentation and
discussion, with separate motions required on the two actions.
The current use of the property is residential, residential vacant land and is
immediately adjacent to either residential, residential vacant, or agricultural land
located in the LU - Land Use zone district.  A portion of the mentioned property is
unplatted while the other is platted as a portion of Tract 1, Pita Ranch.
