### Page 3 of 4

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
April 11, 2024
Shane Hansen, applicants agent, was available to answer questions. Access will be
off Road 146 down what is currently known as Tract 2, Wilson Acres. Tract 2 was
turned into an easement many years ago and is for access into the back lots where all
the property sits right now. It was recorded and dedicated to the public and has been
maintained with things that have been built into the access easement. Road will be
renamed and will take care of maintenance issues.
Chairman Caughey opened the Public Hearing for public comments. Jeffrey Boldt,
attorney for adjoining property owners Tanner and Abigail Leuning said they are the
owners of Tract 2, Wilson Acres, the easement property. They also own Lot 1, Block
1, Thunder Basin Estates, 4th Filing which is the terminus of that easement On the
west side is their house. They have serious concerns, clearly there is a recorded
easement and don't dispute that. While the easement talks about the responsibility for
maintenance this action will go from one family to serving an additional seven families
and before that construction traffic. There has been no attempt by the applicant to
discuss future maintenance of roadway. Client asks that this application not be
approved until the applicant talks about the needed improvements. Also they are
concerned about the naming of the road since the applicant is not the owner of the
easement and they don't particularly like the name selected.
Chairman Caughey closed the hearing. In response to public comments Shane
Hansen said that the road will be built to County road standards all the way to Road
146 and no building permits will be issued until the roads are completed. Maintenance
of the road will be maintained by the internal subdivision. As for naming of the road
that was a recommendation of Laramie County since there were not enough points of
addresses to use Road 146 and suggested the easement be renamed. Justin Arnold
answered questions on naming a road. If all parties  affected by the name change do
not agree then the Commissioners would have to approve the name change. Setback
requirements of current residence should not have issues for the existing home.
A motion was made by Jack Stadel, seconded by John Watkins, to
approve the Preliminary Development Plan for Pita Ranch, 2nd Filing,
situated in a portion of the N1/2 of the SE1/4 of Section 34, Township 14
North, Range 63 West, and a portion of Tract 1, Pita Ranch, Laramie
County, WY and to adopt the findings of fact a of the staff report. Vote 4-0.
Caughey, Stadel, Watkins, Gaspar
Aye:
Smith
Excused:
Recommendation of Pita Ranch, 2nd Filing Subdivision Permit and Plat
John
Watkins
moved,
seconded
by
Natasha
Gaspar
to
recommend
approval of the Subdivision Permit and Plat for Pita Ranch, 2nd Filing to
the Laramie County Board of Commissioners and adopt the findings of
facts b and c of the staff report with the following condition:
